From: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: frontend: suniv: load the 4-tap scaler filter

suniv (F1C100s/F1C200s) ran its frontend scaler with the FIR filter off:
COEF_ACCESS_CTRL left set and no coefficients loaded, because the A10
tables gave a green image. Scaled planes were point-sampled, so a 2x
enlargement looked blocky.

The F1C200s manual (5.2.5.38-41) gives this DEFE 4-tap filters in both
directions: one word per phase at 0x400/0x500 (channel 0) and
0x600/0x700 (channel 1), and nothing at the HORZCOEF1 offsets the A10/A33
8-tap horizontal table also writes. Load the 4-tap vertical table into
all four, and give the coefficient RAM back to the scaler by clearing
COEF_ACCESS_CTRL. At 1:1 phase 0 is [0, 64, 0, 0], so unscaled planes
are unchanged.

OFF BY DEFAULT: on the board the picture still came out green (dead
chroma), 1:1 included. sun4i_frontend.fir=1 turns it on for tests.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_frontend.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_frontend.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_frontend.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_frontend.c
@@ -23,6 +23,10 @@
 #include "sun4i_drv.h"
 #include "sun4i_frontend.h"
 
+static bool sun4i_frontend_fir;
+module_param_named(fir, sun4i_frontend_fir, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(fir, "suniv: filter when scaling (off: chroma came out green)");
+
 static const u32 sun4i_frontend_vert_coef[32] = {
 	0x00004000, 0x000140ff, 0x00033ffe, 0x00043ffd,
 	0x00063efc, 0xff083dfc, 0x000a3bfb, 0xff0d39fb,
@@ -117,15 +121,44 @@
 	int i;
 
 	/*
-	 * suniv (F1C100s/F1C200s): the FIR scaler filter produces working luma
-	 * but dead chroma (whole image green). Allwinner's bare-metal code
-	 * leaves COEF_ACCESS_CTRL set, which bypasses the FIR filter, and loads
-	 * no coefficients. Do the same -- we only need 1:1 video here.
+	 * suniv (F1C100s/F1C200s) has 4-tap filters only, horizontal as well as
+	 * vertical (F1C200s User Manual 5.2.5.38-41): one word per phase at
+	 * 0x400/0x500 (channel 0) and 0x600/0x700 (channel 1), and nothing at
+	 * the HORZCOEF1 offsets. The A10/A33 tables below have an 8-tap
+	 * horizontal filter, which there gave working luma but no chroma (a
+	 * green image). The vertical table is a 4-tap one, so it serves both
+	 * directions. COEF_ACCESS_CTRL gives the coefficient RAM to the CPU
+	 * while it is loaded and back to the scaler after; left set, the
+	 * scaler samples without filtering (blocky when it enlarges).
+	 *
+	 * OFF BY DEFAULT: on the F1C200s this still gave a green picture (dead
+	 * chroma, even at 1:1). sun4i_frontend.fir=1 turns it on for tests; a
+	 * change in sysfs applies only when the frontend next powers up.
 	 */
 	if (frontend->data->scaler_bypass) {
 		regmap_write_bits(frontend->regs, SUN4I_FRONTEND_FRM_CTRL_REG,
 				  SUN4I_FRONTEND_FRM_CTRL_COEF_ACCESS_CTRL,
 				  SUN4I_FRONTEND_FRM_CTRL_COEF_ACCESS_CTRL);
+		if (!sun4i_frontend_fir)
+			return;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < 32; i++) {
+			regmap_write(frontend->regs,
+				     SUN4I_FRONTEND_CH0_HORZCOEF0_REG(i),
+				     sun4i_frontend_vert_coef[i]);
+			regmap_write(frontend->regs,
+				     SUN4I_FRONTEND_CH0_VERTCOEF_REG(i),
+				     sun4i_frontend_vert_coef[i]);
+			regmap_write(frontend->regs,
+				     SUN4I_FRONTEND_CH1_HORZCOEF0_REG(i),
+				     sun4i_frontend_vert_coef[i]);
+			regmap_write(frontend->regs,
+				     SUN4I_FRONTEND_CH1_VERTCOEF_REG(i),
+				     sun4i_frontend_vert_coef[i]);
+		}
+
+		regmap_write_bits(frontend->regs, SUN4I_FRONTEND_FRM_CTRL_REG,
+				  SUN4I_FRONTEND_FRM_CTRL_COEF_ACCESS_CTRL, 0);
 		return;
 	}
 
